hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"932","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Amr bin Ali, and Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, h. Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, all of them on the authority of Hisham, H. Al-Dawrqi narrated to us, Ibn Ulayya narrated to us, H, and Abu Hashim, from us Ismail, who is Ibn Ulayya, from us Ayoub, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Arqam, He was leading his people in prayer, so he came and the prayer had been established, and he said: Let one of you pray, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When the time for prayer has come and the defecation has come, then begin to defecate.” This is the hadith of Abu Kurayb, and the meaning of the text of their hadiths is the same."
